WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.737
Module 7 builds on earlier SQL ideas.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:08.932
You should already recognize basic SELECT queries, aggregate functions, simple joins, and NULL.

00:00:08.932 --> 00:00:14.212
Subqueries combine those familiar pieces in a new structure.

00:00:14.212 --> 00:00:19.137
If you can read a simple query on its own, the main new skill is understanding how the

00:00:19.137 --> 00:00:24.367
result of one query is used by another.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:30.147
Connect this idea to a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists.

00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:35.872
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.872 --> 00:00:43.542
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:49.552
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.552 --> 00:00:55.571
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
